  "description": "Mending a worn or frayed board corner on an existing binding. The damaged corner is glued and tapped firm and square with a hammer, allowed to dry hard, and then a small slip of matching new leather is worked in under the lifted old covering before the corner is re-covered. The aim is a sound corner that disappears into the original surface.",
